{
  "compilerOptions": {
    /* Base Options: */
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "target": "ES2022",
    "allowJs": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "moduleDetection": "force",
    "isolatedModules": true,

    /* Strictness */
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,

    /* NodeNext = TypeScript's current recommended setting for Node.js projects (not the legacy
       "Node10" resolver) — it applies Node's real module-resolution algorithm (package.json
       "exports" fields, conditional exports, etc.), and picks CJS vs ESM output per-file based on
       the nearest package.json's "type" field. This package.json has no "type": "module", so output
       is CommonJS (see adapters/swagger/index.ts's __dirname comment for the concrete consequence)
       — matches oingg-tpex-ts/oingg-tdcc-ts/oingg-sitca-ts, same tsconfig shape.

       Paired with `paths` below + `tsc-alias` in the build script: imports use the `@/*` alias, not
       relative paths, so NodeNext's "relative imports need an explicit .js extension" rule never
       applies to them in source — tsc-alias adds the correct extension when it rewrites the alias to
       a relative path in the compiled output. Discovered 2026-09-01 while building the Dockerfile for
       the first real deploy: this project's imports were extensionless relative paths, which tsx
       (dev) resolves fine but plain `node dist/index.js` (prod, no bundler) rejected with
       ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND — switching to the `@/*` + tsc-alias pattern fixed it without having to
       hand-edit every import statement in the codebase to add `.js` extensions. */
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["./src/*"]
    },

    /* TypeScript 7 把 types 的預設改成 []，不再自動載入 node_modules/@types 底下的全部套件。現在不寫也能
       過，只是因為有檔案 import node:stream 之類的模組、連帶把 @types/node 的全域宣告（process、Buffer）
       帶進來——那是巧合，不是設定。明確寫出來，單獨用 process 的檔案才不會依賴別的檔案的 import。 */
    "types": ["node"],

    /* Build options */
    "outDir": "dist",
    "rootDir": "src"
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist"]
}
